# Local Postgres started by `docker compose up postgres` at repo root.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://crumb:crumb@localhost:5432/crumb

# Tip: any var below also accepts a `<VAR>_FILE` companion pointing at a file
# whose contents are the value (Docker/Kubernetes secrets convention). The
# Docker entrypoint loads it at startup unless the var is set directly —
# e.g. DATABASE_URL_FILE=/run/secrets/db_url. See the README "Secrets from files".

# ─── Tier ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "self_host" (default): OSS deployment. AGPL. Free. Email goes to stdout.
#                        Integrations work if you BYO OAuth-app creds.
#                        AI + Session Record are Cloud-only (off here).
# "cloud":               the hosted tier at crumb.localhostlabs.net. Enables managed
#                        email + makes AI / Session Record / integrations
#                        available — gated per-workspace by Stripe plan
#                        (see lib/entitlements.ts).
# CRUMB_TIER=self_host

# ─── Public origin ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical public origin of this dashboard. When set, it's used to build every
# OAuth integration callback (`{CRUMB_APP_URL}/api/integrations/<provider>/callback`)
# instead of guessing from x-forwarded-host — the recommended single knob behind
# a proxy / load balancer. Precedence: CRUMB_APP_URL → per-provider *_REDIRECT_URL
# → request host. Register the matching callback URL in each provider's app.
# CRUMB_APP_URL=https://app.yourdomain.com

# ─── Secret encryption at rest ──────────────────────────────
# Encrypts third-party integration tokens (Slack / Linear / Jira) before
# they're written to the workspaces table, using AES-256-GCM. Strongly
# recommended for Cloud; optional for single-node self-host. When unset,
# tokens are stored in plaintext (a startup warning is logged).
#
# Value is 32 bytes — 64 hex chars or base64. Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# After setting it on an existing deployment, encrypt already-stored tokens:
#   pnpm --filter @crumb/db exec tsx src/backfill-encrypt-secrets.ts
#
# Rotation: bump CRUMB_ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID and add the prior key as
# CRUMB_ENCRYPTION_KEY_<oldId> so existing ciphertext still decrypts, then
# re-run the backfill to re-seal under the new key.
# CRUMB_ENCRYPTION_KEY=...
# CRUMB_ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID=1

# ─── Logging & error tracking ───────────────────────────────
# Structured JSON logs go to stdout/stderr. Level: debug | info | warn |
# error. Defaults to "info" in production, "debug" otherwise.
# CRUMB_LOG_LEVEL=info
#
# Optional error tracking. When set, log.error() forwards exceptions to
# Sentry. Requires @sentry/node to be installed (Cloud bundles it; self-host
# can `pnpm add @sentry/node`). Unset = no-op, no dependency needed.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://...ingest.sentry.io/...

# ─── Storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where attachment + Session Record bytes live.
#   "local" (default): per-instance disk under CRUMB_STORAGE_DIR. Fine for
#                      single-node self-host.
#   "postgres":        bytes stored in the DB (base64 text) so a multi-
#                      instance Cloud deployment shares storage. Required
#                      for Cloud; S3/R2 is a future adapter.
# CRUMB_STORAGE_PROVIDER=local

# ─── Scaling (multi-instance Cloud) ─────────────────────────
# When set, the rate limiter uses a shared Redis token bucket instead of a
# per-process in-memory one — required if you run more than one app instance
# behind a load balancer (otherwise each box enforces its own copy of the
# limit). Requires ioredis to be installed (Cloud bundles it). Unset = the
# in-memory limiter, correct for single-node self-host. Falls back to
# in-memory automatically if Redis is unreachable.
# CRUMB_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# ─── Email delivery ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Default is "stdout" — magic-link emails print to the dashboard's log.
# Fine for dev / first-run; not deliverable.
#
# Managed email via Resend requires CRUMB_TIER=cloud:
# CRUMB_EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# CRUMB_EMAIL_FROM="Crumb <crumb@yourdomain.com>"

# ─── Slack integration (vendor notifications) ───────────────
# Workspace admins click "Connect Slack" in Settings → Integrations to
# install. Customer replies on items they own (or all admins, if
# unassigned) then DM the right teammate when they pick "Slack" as their
# delivery channel.
#
# Cloud: we hold creds; self-host: register your own app at
# https://api.slack.com/apps with scopes:
#   chat:write, im:write, users:read, users:read.email
# and set the OAuth redirect URL to
#   {dashboard origin}/api/integrations/slack/callback
# SLACK_CLIENT_ID=...
# SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# Optional override when host detection is unreliable (e.g. behind a tunnel):
# SLACK_REDIRECT_URL=https://your-dashboard.example.com/api/integrations/slack/callback
# Optional HMAC key for signed OAuth state (falls back to CRUMB_INBOUND_SECRET → SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET):
# SLACK_STATE_SECRET=...
# /crumb slash command (create a Crumb item from Slack): add the "commands"
# scope, point the command + interactivity Request URLs at
#   {origin}/api/integrations/slack/commands  and  .../slack/interactivity
# and set the app's signing secret so we can verify those requests:
# SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=...

# ─── Engineering integrations (Phase 9) ─────────────────────
# Cloud holds creds; self-host BYO. All three providers share the same
# pattern: workspace-level install, manual ticket create from a thread,
# webhook status sync. AI drafting (Cloud + AISTACK_API_KEY) pulls
# recent ticket titles from the target + the GitHub repo's README +
# top-level tree (if installed) for voice context.
#
# Optional CRUMB_OAUTH_STATE_SECRET overrides the shared HMAC key used
# for OAuth state signing (falls back to CRUMB_INBOUND_SECRET, then any
# of the provider client secrets).
# CRUMB_OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=...

# Linear (OAuth 2.0). Register at linear.app/settings/api → Developer.
# Redirect URL: {dashboard origin}/api/integrations/linear/callback
# LINEAR_CLIENT_ID=...
# LINEAR_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# LINEAR_REDIRECT_URL=https://your-dashboard.example.com/api/integrations/linear/callback   # optional, only if x-forwarded-host is unreliable
# LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...   # configured at the Linear app's Webhooks page

# Jira (Atlassian Cloud 3LO). Register at developer.atlassian.com.
# Redirect URL: {dashboard origin}/api/integrations/jira/callback
# Scopes: read:jira-work, write:jira-work, read:jira-user, offline_access
# JIRA_CLIENT_ID=...
# JIRA_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# JIRA_REDIRECT_URL=https://your-dashboard.example.com/api/integrations/jira/callback   # optional
# JIRA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...   # configured on the Atlassian webhook

# GitHub App (per-installation, not OAuth user). Register at
# github.com/settings/apps. Webhook URL: {dashboard origin}/api/integrations/github/webhook
# Callback URL:  {dashboard origin}/api/integrations/github/callback
# Permissions: Issues (R/W), Contents (R, for README + tree), Metadata (R)
# Events: Issues
# GITHUB_APP_ID=12345
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=crumb-dashboard
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n"
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...

# ─── AI clustering + ticket drafting (Cloud only) ───────────
# When set + CRUMB_TIER=cloud, new items are auto-classified against the
# workspace's initiatives and surface as accept/dismiss suggestions in
# the inbox + thread sidebar. Vendors can also batch-cluster from the
# inbox "Cluster selected" button. The same model drafts engineering
# tickets. Talks to an OpenAI-compatible aistack endpoint.
# AISTACK_API_KEY=sk-aistack-xxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# AISTACK_BASE_URL=https://aistack.eissa.cloud/v1   # optional; this is the default
# AISTACK_MODEL=qwen-35b-8bit                       # optional; default qwen-35b-8bit (128K ctx)
#
# Embeddings power semantic dedup, "Ask your feedback", and churn retrieval.
# Served at the same aistack host (returns 1024-dim, matching the pgvector
# column), so it works out of the box once AISTACK_API_KEY is set — no extra
# config. Override ONLY if the embedding model is served elsewhere:
# AISTACK_EMBEDDINGS_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-8B   # optional; this is the default
# EMBEDDINGS_BASE_URL=https://aistack.eissa.cloud/v1  # optional; defaults to AISTACK_BASE_URL

# ─── Cost controls (Cloud) ──────────────────────────────────
# Per-workspace MONTHLY caps, metered in the usage_counters table and reset
# on the 1st (UTC) automatically. Defaults are per-plan (see lib/usage.ts);
# these env vars override the paid-plan defaults across the board.
#   AI ops/month (clustering + ticket drafts):   team 2000, growth 10000
# CRUMB_AI_MONTHLY_CAP=10000
#   Replay storage MB/month (growth only):        5120 (5 GB)
# CRUMB_REPLAY_MONTHLY_MB=5120
#
# Plan-aware replay RETENTION (prunes sessions older than N days via the
# cleanup endpoint below). OPT-IN — unset means keep replays forever. Global
# default + optional per-plan overrides (…_GROWTH / _TEAM / _FREE):
# CRUMB_REPLAY_RETENTION_DAYS=90
# CRUMB_REPLAY_RETENTION_DAYS_GROWTH=90

# ─── Maintenance / cron ─────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret for the internal cleanup endpoint, which prunes orphans:
# replay sessions that never linked to an item + attachments uploaded but
# never linked to a reply. The endpoint 503s until this is set. Wire any
# cron (Vercel Cron, GitHub Actions, k8s CronJob) to:
#   curl -X POST -H "X-Crumb-Sweep-Secret: $CRUMB_INTERNAL_SWEEP_SECRET" \
#     https://your-crumb-host/api/v1/internal/replay-sweep
# CRUMB_INTERNAL_SWEEP_SECRET=...

# ─── Inbound email (reply-by-email + forward-to-capture) ────
# CRUMB_INBOUND_DOMAIN is the domain your mail provider routes to the inbound
# webhooks (Resend Inbound / SendGrid Parse / Mailgun / Postmark → POST JSON).
# Two flows:
#   - reply-by-email: a customer replies to a notification email and it lands
#     on the thread (reply+<FB-id>.<token>@DOMAIN → /api/v1/inbound/reply).
#   - forward-to-capture: forward any customer email to
#     inbox+<workspace-slug>.<token>@DOMAIN → a pending capture in /captures
#     (on Cloud, an AI account suggestion is attached for one-click confirm).
# CRUMB_INBOUND_SECRET signs those addresses (HMAC) and optionally gates the
# webhook (Authorization: Bearer <secret>). Generate: openssl rand -hex 32.
# CRUMB_INBOUND_DOMAIN=reply.yourdomain.com
# CRUMB_INBOUND_SECRET=...
